.TH IAD\-ADAPTIVE\-SPLIT 3 "" "iced-adaptive-design 0.1.0" "iced-adaptive-design Manual"
.SH NAME
adaptive_split \- The adaptive sidebar: beside the content when there is room, a drawer when there is not, and one continuous motion between the two
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
adaptive_split(sidebar: impl Into<Element<'a, M, Theme>>, content: impl Into<Element<'a, M, Theme>>, wide: bool, sidebar_width: f32, drawer_width: f32)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The adaptive sidebar: beside the content when there is room, a drawer when there is not, and one continuous motion between the two.
.PP
The sidebar is a single child that lives in one of two places:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBin flow\fR: it takes space at the start edge and displaces the content;
.IP \(bu 2
\fBas a drawer\fR: it floats over the content on a scrim.
.PP
Both use the sidebar spring (damping ratio 1, mass 0.5, stiffness 500), so a window crossing the collapse breakpoint slides the sidebar out of (or into) the layout the same way the drawer slides over the content. The only difference is the layer: in flow the content moves out of its way instead of being covered.
.SH FUNCTIONS
.TP
.B adaptive_split(sidebar: impl Into<Element<'a, M, Theme>>, content: impl Into<Element<'a, M, Theme>>, wide: bool, sidebar_width: f32, drawer_width: f32)
A sidebar and a content area. \fBwide\fR: the sidebar sits beside the content (\fBsidebar_width\fR); otherwise it is a drawer (\fBdrawer_width\fR) shown while \fBdrawer_open\fR.
.SH PROPERTIES
Builder methods, chained after the constructor.
.TP
.B \&.drawer_open(open: bool)
.TP
.B \&.side(side: Side)
The edge the sidebar is docked to (default the start edge, \fBLeft\fR): it slides in from it, and the content gives way on that side. \fBRight\fR is an aside, \fBTop\fR and \fBBottom\fR a bar or a sheet. Not mirrored for right\-to\-left text.
.TP
.B \&.extent(extent: Extent)
Sizes the sidebar by an \fBExtent\fR resolved at layout (its own size, a fraction of the room) instead of the widths given to \fBadaptive_split\fR; both the in\-flow panel and the drawer take it.
.TP
.B \&.window_radius(r: f32)
Rounds the drawer scrim to the window's corners.
.SH EVENTS
